{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat method.py; cat solve.sh; cat research_journal.md; cat method_notes.json'","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"Denoised graph-seasonal networks and median residual corrections.\"\"\"\nimport conditional_calibration\n\n\ndef fit(features, targets, seed):\n    return conditional_calibration.fit(features, targets, seed, site_head='graph',\n                                       gate_mode='site_neighbor_horizon', network_replicas=2,\n                                       network_epochs=(100, 80), network_diffusion=True,\n                                       residual_tree='diffused')\n\n\ndef predict(state, features):\n    return conditional_calibration.predict(state, features)\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\npython /opt/forecast-engine/evaluate.py --solution /workspace/solution\n# Forecasting research journal\n\n## Active resumed turn, 2026-10-06 16:49 UTC\nRead `/workspace/instruction.md`, `/workspace/task.toml`, the entry point and this journal. The required unchanged initial `./solve.sh` attempt returned **HTTP 409 Conflict** immediately, with no fit or trusted metric; this is an infrastructure failure, not a method result. Retained public best remains 13.924304561281838. Own calibration caches and source backups are under `/tmp/forecast_turn_residual/`. Next: verify the suggested 0.35 residual multiplier locally, then test a substantive compact trajectory/context design for the shallow OOF residual tree; preserve the complete winner until a real public comparison is available.\n\nCalibration diagnostics use the existing seed-17 origin blocks and matching OOF expert/gate predictions, never development labels. Original residual-tree control: **13.3281924488 / 13.0908108395** (last/middle). Multiplier 0.35 worsens to 13.3317699580 / 13.0966801878; 0.65 improves to 13.3256321083 / 13.0859476374 but is only a scalar diagnostic, not the structural candidate. Compact expert-trajectory features (persistent gaps, means/end-point changes, local slopes), graph neighbor summaries, flow, clock and normalized expert inputs all fail to improve both blocks; slopes leave predictions exactly unchanged. A 64-member randomized forest with clipped-error squared-loss splits and recomputed median leaf values, either replacing or equally blending the shallow residual tree, also worsens both blocks (best ensemble 13.3392429549 / 13.1009714520).\n\nImplemented structural candidate: retain the six expert inputs and add **two bounded signed anchor/base and recent-history/base differences**, normalized by per-origin mean history with floor 30. Same OOF residual targets, shallow median boosting and half-strength bounded correction. Calibration **13.3280645312 / 13.0894228932**, small improvements on both. `method.py` now activates `residual_tree='signed_context'`; public evaluation successfully launched at 16:55 UTC after a second unchanged HTTP 409, result pending. Source backups preserve the 13.9243045613 winner; revert the wrapper if the complete masked MAE does not improve.\n\nSigned-context public result **13.925918911711555**, score 3.160403670610135, evaluation `876d68f97845431093b0992d4907bc87`, seeds 17/29/43 and all gates pass. Worse by 0.0016143504: **reverted both method and helper source**. The restored winner was rerun: **13.924304561281838**, score 3.163814238553845, evaluation `99ce6f93b2e344a489e72927595c2742`, all seeds/gates pass, exactly repeats prior best.\n\nAdditional rejected calibration experiments: weighted-LAD nonlinear tree expert gate (13.3401416175 / 13.0927351402 with original residual tree); graph clusters/coordinates as residual features are unused, replacing sensor category with coordinates worsens to 13.3424302323 / 13.0996886113; full-batch convex refit of network output/graph-seasonal layers lowers its training objective but gives mixed final MAE 13.3398273343 / 13.0839834395. Learned shared, signed-gap and graph-sensor gates **between the two network replicas**, with origin-cross-fitted pair predictions then refitted diffusion/gate/residual tree, all worsen middle: respectively 13.3274567462 / 13.0937732394, 13.3275957989 / 13.0945961518, 13.3281272326 / 13.0944232410. Keep equal averaging. Learning final residual strength from three additional residual-tree origin cross-fits (horizon, correction-magnitude or signed-context inputs) prefers smaller strengths around 0.4 and worsens both outer blocks. These are actual calibration diagnostics, not public scores.\n\nNew structural candidate **final residual-tree spatial denoising with seasonal preservation, at full strength**. Fit a sensor/horizon/two-harmonic projection to the shallow residual-tree's calibration predictions; diffuse 25% of scale-normalized innovations over the same learned history graph while preserving this projection, then add the resulting correction. Original inputs, cross-fitted residual targets and +/-10 pre-diffusion cap stay. Calibration control (half-strength): 13.3281924488 / 13.0908108395; undenoised full-strength: 13.3245466895 / 13.0795544989; raw-denoised full-strength: 13.3239231543 / 13.0780949140; **seasonal-denoised full-strength: 13.3225855637 / 13.0773360887**. Thus the denoiser itself improves both over the full-strength control. Implementation exactly matches prototype predictions on both blocks (max difference 0). Active wrapper uses `residual_tree='diffused'`; complete public evaluation launched 17:16 UTC, pending. Seed-29 fresh-fit runtime and independent reload verification are also in progress. Keep backup `/tmp/forecast_turn_residual/{method,conditional}.best` until public masked MAE beats 13.9243045613.\n\n## Best and protocol\nRetained best: **13.924304561281838 masked MAE**, score **3.163814238553845**, evaluation `a5617cbb56d2418baf5e32ab096e383e`, seeds **17/29/43**, all quality gates passed. `method.py` is the runnable graph-seasonal network / median-tree ensemble with graph-regularized sensor, signed-disagreement, horizon and neighbor gates. This turn started 2026-10-06 15:43 UTC by reading the task rules and this journal, then running the unchanged entry point. Its previously pending combined gate improves the prior best 13.976312484716415 by **0.003435284870527**.\n\nAll public numbers are actual complete `./solve.sh` responses, fresh fits and independent checkpoint reloads under the unchanged seed protocol. Only calibration labels and public features accessed; no development targets, held-out/reference material, other track, target reconstruction, downloads, scorer or frozen edits. Sixteen Python source files; one BLAS/OpenMP thread per active fit, never more than two active CPU threads. Public asset hashes match the manifest. Frozen solve.sh SHA-256: `d6e0c77a5c20b1afee86cdc5576402b45fea48f5623a0729b3c748d2ee5b4a4a`.\n\n## Method\nTrees: absolute-error HistGradientBoosting, 90 stages, 15 leaves, leaf minimum 250, L2 20. Equally blend pooled and horizon 1-6 / 7-12 specialists. Inputs include base, historical anchors, history summaries, forecast slopes, clock/horizon/sensor, and eight neighbors learned from within-history change correlations.\n\nNetwork: 6D sensor embedding, 48/24 tanh layers, linear skip, two daily Fourier harmonics, smooth absolute loss (2 units), 100 Adam epochs / batch 4096. Sensor intercept/horizon/periodic head uses ridge 0.0005 and learned-neighbor Laplacian 0.005 on periodic coefficients.\n\nThree contiguous-origin cross-fits train the sigmoid expert gate. Inputs include horizon, bounded absolute/signed anchor and recent-history disagreement, variability, expert gap, flow, four horizon interactions, signed expert-gap x horizon and scale-normalized neighbor expert gap. Centered sensor coefficients have ridge 0.02 and graph Laplacian 0.05; prior network weights 0.18 short / 0.32 long, clipped [0.05,0.65].\n\nRuntime repair from prior turn: two-thread fit used 201.339 CPU seconds and failed the 180-second CPU bound. One-thread control uses **88.164 wall / 87.219 CPU seconds**, all 100 epochs. Its 793,713-byte checkpoint independently reloaded in 5.849 seconds with zero discrepancy and finite `(148,12,170)` output. One-thread control MAE 13.977059216214395 differs from prior two-thread forecast by only 1.02e-7.\n\n## Current turn experiments\nCalibration diagnostics: seed 17; train 0:50 / test 50:74 (last), train 0:25 plus 49:74 / test 25:49 (middle). Matching inner OOF excludes test origins. Caches/scripts in `/tmp/forecast_turn_graph/` are our own calibration work, not trusted scores.\n\n| Implemented method | Last MAE | Middle MAE | Decision |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | --- |\n| Signed expert-gap gate | 13.3903562853 | 13.1157889789 | Prior public best |\n| Combined neighbor/horizon gate | 13.3835978916 | 13.1110341605 | Public best 13.9728771998 |\n| Graph-sharing network horizon head, signed-gap gate | 13.3923195392 | 13.1113203922 | Mixed; defer |\n| Graph-sharing network horizon head, combined gate | 13.3840290434 | 13.1062592204 | Mixed; defer |\n| OOF residual shared bias/horizon, combined gate | 13.3880373480 | 13.1187796788 | Reject |\n| OOF graph sensor bias/horizon, combined gate | 13.3893910043 | 13.1279567944 | Reject |\n| OOF graph sensor seasonal residual, combined gate | 13.4808458920 | 13.1144020215 | Reject |\n| OOF graph sensor seasonal/context residual, combined gate | 13.4787264540 | 13.1155112003 | Reject |\n| Two independent networks, signed-gap gate | 13.3686053574 | 13.1015282284 | Improved both |\n| Two independent networks, combined gate | 13.3633204147 | 13.1005217184 | Public candidate |\n| Ensemble + shared replica disagreement gate | 13.3632664402 | 13.1012185187 | Mixed; defer |\n| Ensemble + sensor replica disagreement gate | 13.3646321162 | 13.1023274516 | Reject |\n| Original + sensor-scale-normalized network | 13.4184039446 | 13.1269929710 | Reject |\n| Ensemble + raw spatial diffusion | 13.3489960174 | 13.1008413423 | Mixed; defer |\n| Ensemble + seasonal-preserving spatial diffusion | 13.3454756862 | 13.0992632572 | Improved both; next public candidate |\n\nResidual head fitted smooth absolute loss on cross-fitted final expert errors with shared and centered sensor coefficients, graph sharing and bounded +/-20 correction. Signed-gap controls also worsened on both blocks (shared 13.3932177724 / 13.1251443144; sensor 13.3944925704 / 13.1357166148; seasonal 13.4869654677 / 13.1247434966; context 13.4846206127 / 13.1257130217). Implementation was reverted.\n\nIn progress: **two independent network initializations**, seeds s and s+1009, average their predictions in every OOF fold and full fit, then refit the same gate. `method.py` now tests `network_replicas=2`; retained one-network wrapper is `/tmp/forecast_turn_graph/method.neighbor_horizon_best`. Pure network last/middle MAE improves 13.7037773132 / 13.7623052597 -> 13.5825910568 / 13.5900487900. Initial full seed-17 candidate fit used **161.505 wall / 160.865 CPU seconds**, both 100-epoch members; state **849,704 bytes**, finite `(148,12,170)` output. Independent reload took 5.846 seconds with zero discrepancy. However protected run `a94a1b3bc86841078689de84b1125c6f` returned **execution_error, no metric**. Runtime proximity is a suspected cause, not confirmed by the public response.\n\nRuntime repair in progress: node gradients now use `bincount` accumulation (microbenchmark 0.0506 vs 0.2856 milliseconds per 4096x6 batch, maximum float32 aggregation difference 2.86e-6); backprop multiplies only the six embedding columns instead of computing unused input gradients. Fixed epochs, objectives and model architecture remain. Full local seeds 17/43 are being checked before the protected retry. Shared and sensor-specific replica-disagreement gates did not improve both blocks and are inactive.\n\nSensor-scale-normalized neural residuals used history-only graph scales and per-row loss weights to preserve raw MAE; replacing the second replica worsened both blocks and is inactive. Spatial diffusion splits cross-fitted network corrections into sensor intercept/horizon/two-harmonic seasonal projection and innovations. It diffuses 25% of normalized innovations over the eight learned neighbors, preserves sensor seasonal terms, then refits the original expert gate. Seasonal coefficients are fitted to forecasts, not labels; all training targets still enter only the experts/gate. Implementation in `spatial_calibration.diffusion_fit/predict` reproduces the two block scores above; raw diffusion without the seasonal separation failed to improve both. Diffusion is not yet active in method.py.\n\n## Protected result history\nEvery successful public run passed all quality gates.\n\n| Method | Complete masked MAE | Outcome |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Initial identity | 15.4218571566 | Baseline |\n| Robust pooled/sensor linear | 15.0648913575 | Superseded |\n| Median trees 90 / 180 stages | 14.1452638897 / 14.1455193190 | 180 rejected |\n| Learned-neighbor tree | 14.1214289791 | Superseded |\n| Neighbor tree + sensor affine | 14.1433545829 | Reject despite local gain |\n| Seasonal innovations | 14.1209047365 | Superseded |\n| Pooled/horizon trees | 14.1101708074 | Superseded |\n| Trees + 25% network | 14.0354537227 | Superseded |\n| Cross-fitted neural correction | 14.0429518732 | Reject despite local gain |\n| Horizon-scheduled network | 14.0302026105 | Superseded |\n| Unheaded network + gate | 14.0180263118 | Superseded; exact repeat |\n| Summary/relative-history ensemble | 14.0312982042 | Reject |\n| Independent seasonal head + gate | 14.0201794624 | Reject |\n| Graph-seasonal head + standard gate | 14.0076506609 | Superseded |\n| Graph head + horizon interactions | 14.0054323900 | Superseded |\n| Sensor/horizon gate | 13.9928520282 | Superseded |\n| Sensor absolute-context gate | 13.9782379197 | Superseded; exact repeat |\n| Sensor signed-context gate | 13.9770593182 | Superseded |\n| One-thread signed-context control | 13.9770592162 | Runtime repair; `d4846a4a62b948868702aba4623fcbd1` |\n| Sensor signed expert gap | 13.9763124847 | Superseded; `7000ee87cb55466b9e5ea3f6548d436f` |\n| Combined signed gap/horizon/neighbor gate | **13.9728771998** | Retain; `8e114646856644a69066500d2d87f97d` |\n\n## Prior rejected experiments and lessons\nDo not repeat tree history lags/sensor profiles, robust summaries, heteroscedastic residual scaling, neighbor seasonal innovations, three horizon groups, origin-bootstrap trees, physical-graph substitution, short-training network, chronological/relative-history network, epoch averaging, directional expert-distance gates, innovation sensor head, embedding graph regularization, periodic shared gate, correction amplitude or bootstrap gates. Four network-wide context summaries failed last/middle at 13.4490161498 / 13.2626610405. Sensor variability/absolute expert-gap reliability failed both blocks. Rich history and independent seasonal heads failed public scoring despite local gains. Graph sharing of periodic coefficients transfers better. Public feature-only development anchor disagreement tails are wider; keep relative variables bounded.\n\n## Next discriminating experiment\nFinish runtime repair and retry the two-initialization ensemble under the complete public protocol. If it improves, test the already-implemented seasonal-preserving spatial denoiser under the same protocol, retaining strictly by actual MAE. A later distinct experiment is a small joint 12-horizon residual network as a complementary expert; fixed post-hoc horizon smoothing failed previously, so use a learned trajectory model and both origin blocks. End by rerunning the retained best and updating method_notes.json to match the actual entry point.\n\n## Resumed turn, 2026-10-06\nRead the rules and this journal, then launched the unchanged entry point (two networks, 100/80 epochs) through `./solve.sh`; result pending. Calibration caches confirm this budgeted ensemble at 13.3611750031 / 13.1145311229, with seasonal-preserving network diffusion at 13.3429248512 / 13.1133855353. Full cached seeds 17/43 use 100/100 epochs; seed 29 uses 100/80. Do not confuse their runtime artifacts with the current wrapper.\n\nJoint 12-horizon trajectory network (48/24 hidden layers, shared graph-seasonal head, 100 epochs) is rejected: pure network 14.8138484955 / 14.7481040955; adding it as a third equal network member yields 13.4069144933 / 13.1590245472 without diffusion and 13.3965151141 / 13.1555658812 with diffusion. Both blocks worsen. Tree-only seasonal-preserving diffusion gives 13.3631790136 / 13.1107762363 (mixed); diffusing both experts gives 13.3622924089 / 13.1231502401 (worse than network-only diffusion on both). These are calibration diagnostics, not protected scores. Smaller 32/16 networks are being checked as a compute-budgeted diversity experiment; scripts and own caches are in `/tmp/forecast_turn_resume/`.\n\nUnchanged initial entry point passed complete seeds 17/29/43 at **13.966280749980996**, score **3.07513297026098**, all quality gates passed, evaluation `b1ac965e7ba04252b9c01eeaf090e310`. Retain the two-network 100/80-epoch ensemble: gain 0.006596449864892 against prior 13.972877199845888. Control wrapper saved in `/tmp/forecast_turn_resume/method.best`. `method.py` now enables seasonal-preserving network diffusion; public result pending. Three narrower 32/16 networks failed both blocks (13.3740181680 / 13.1455490444 without diffusion; 13.3576780346 / 13.1366649564 with diffusion). One wide plus two narrow members also failed (13.3843641102 / 13.1214535203; diffused 13.3620302494 / 13.1203179147). Both architectural alternatives stay inactive.\n\nSeasonal-preserving network diffusion public result: **13.9474322555024**, score **3.1149533648125804**, evaluation `973b35ab3ae24c0694d4fe98554abcf8`; it improves the 13.966280749981 baseline by 0.0188484944786. Independent reload was exact (max difference 0), finite shape `(148,12,170)`, and the seed-29 local fit used 143.7 wall / 140.8 CPU seconds with a 923,314-byte state.\n\nA 40-stage shallow median residual tree (7 leaves, minimum leaf 2000, L2 50, LR 0.05) improves both origin blocks after network diffusion. The six inputs are horizon, categorical sensor, tree-minus-base, network-minus-base, network-minus-tree and blend-minus-base. Targets are errors after a separately origin-cross-fitted gate on the primary OOF predictions. Half-strength corrections are clipped to +/-10. Calibration expert-only 13.3281924488 / 13.0908108395 versus diffused control 13.3429248512 / 13.1133855353; broad original context instead gives 13.3367063338 / 13.0941527260. Optional `residual_tree=True` in `conditional_calibration.fit` reproduces the expert-only values exactly. Full seed-29 runtime/reload check is pending; this stage is not yet active in method.py.\n\nThe residual-tree candidate is now active in `method.py` for public evaluation. Its local stage is intentionally half-strength and capped; if the complete result does not improve 13.9474322555, revert only `residual_tree=True` and keep diffusion.\n\nResidual-tree public result: **13.924304561281838**, score **3.163814238553845**, evaluation `a5617cbb56d2418baf5e32ab096e383e`; all quality gates passed. This improves diffusion-only 13.9474322555 by 0.0231276942 and the previous 13.9662807500 by 0.0419761887. The retained entry point is two independent graph-seasonal networks (100/80 epochs), seasonal-preserving network diffusion, the cross-fitted neighbor/horizon gate, then the six-input shallow median residual tree at half strength.\n\nNext discriminating experiment: evaluate a lower residual-tree correction multiplier (0.35 versus retained 0.5) on both origin blocks, then only public-score it if both improve; otherwise leave the complete public winner unchanged. Keep the joint trajectory and narrow-network ensembles rejected.\n{\n  \"policy_name\": \"diffused_graph_ensemble_residual_tree\",\n  \"method_summary\": \"Averages two independently initialized graph-seasonal residual networks, diffuses their cross-fitted innovations over learned history neighbors while preserving horizon and daily seasonal terms, blends them with median residual trees through the graph sensor-neighbor-horizon gate, and applies a shallow six-input median residual tree at half strength. The complete three-seed public evaluation confirms MAE 13.9243045613 versus 13.9474322555 without the residual tree and 13.9662807500 before diffusion, with all quality gates passing.\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
